---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getLastUpdated } from "../lib/git-date";
const lastUpdated = getLastUpdated("src/pages/data-deletion.astro");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Data Deletion"
  description="Data deletion instructions for Titanic Quarter Cycling Club."
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
>
  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 prose prose-invert prose-tqcc">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Data Deletion</h1>

      <p>
        Titanic Quarter Cycling Club does not collect, store, or process any personal data from
        visitors to our website. Our use of the Instagram API is limited to displaying posts
        from our own club account. No visitor authentication or login is required.
      </p>

      <h2>Requesting data deletion</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe we hold any personal data about you and would like to request its deletion,
        please email us at
        <a href="mailto:titanicquartercc@gmail.com">titanicquartercc@gmail.com</a>.
        We will respond to your request within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Clearing local data</h2>
      <p>
        Our website stores some preferences (such as unit settings and cookie consent) in your
        browser's local storage. This data is stored only on your device and is never sent to us.
        You can clear it at any time through your browser settings by clearing local storage and
        cookies for this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Managing your Instagram data</h2>
      <p>
        If you wish to manage or delete data associated with your Instagram account, you can do so
        directly through your
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/accounts/privacy_and_security/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Instagram privacy and security settings</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics data</h2>
      <p>
        If you previously accepted analytics cookies, data may have been collected by Google Analytics
        and Microsoft Clarity. You can opt out at any time using the "Manage cookies" link in the
        footer. To request deletion of previously collected analytics data, please contact us and we
        will make reasonable efforts to remove it from these services.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
